// System libraries the Rust bridge needs on iOS.
//
// The archive itself is no longer linked here. Cargokit builds it as part of
// the pod (see rust_builder/ios/websave_bridge.podspec) and force-loads it
// from BUILT_PRODUCTS_DIR, so declaring our own -force_load against a
// hand-built copy under target/ would link the same symbols twice — and would
// quietly use a stale archive whenever build_rust_ios.sh had not been re-run.
//
// -force_load stays necessary, it is just cargokit's job now. Worth knowing
// why: nothing in the Swift or Objective-C references these symbols, because
// Dart looks them up at runtime, so without it the linker drops the whole
// archive as dead weight and the app launches only to fail finding them.
//
// What cargokit does not supply is the set of system libraries core's
// dependencies pull in: libc++ and SQLite via rusqlite, resolv for DNS, and
// Security plus SystemConfiguration for rustls' platform verifier. A Rust
// staticlib records those as link directives cargo has no way to pass on to
// Xcode, so they are named here.

OTHER_LDFLAGS = $(inherited) -lc++ -lresolv -framework Security -framework SystemConfiguration
